# Project Rules — gatekeyp workspace

## Skills system
- Before any task, skim `skills_manifest.md` (see "Installed Skills" table) and check
  `docs/project_memory.md` (per the `project-memory` skill) for relevant lessons.
- Skill sources: legacy guidance files live in `skills/*.md` (Karpathy guidelines, security
  audit, insecure defaults, supply-chain, modern python, property-based testing, UI/UX).
  Web/frontend skills live in `.cline/skills/<name>/SKILL.md` and are auto-discovered:
  `frontend-design`, `web-artifacts-builder`, `webapp-testing`, and the pattern-catalog
  coach `augmented-coding-coach` (sources `vendor/augmented-coding-patterns/`, the Claudia
  fork of augmented-coding-patterns — 66 files of patterns/anti-patterns/obstacles).
- Invoke the matching approach explicitly when asked: "security audit", "audit dependencies",
  "design the UI", "test the web app", etc.

## Process hygiene (mandatory)
- Long/leaky process risks: see **TOP RULES → "Process hygiene"** at the top of
  `docs/project_memory.md`. In short: every `start_process`/`start_search` must be drained
  and terminated before finishing a task; run `list_sessions` + `list_processes` as a
  cleanup audit at end of session; close Playwright/Chromium tabs (`browser_close`) after
  browser debugging; never write loops without a proven exit condition.

## Quality gates (run manually or via pre-commit — no MCP server behind these)
- Vulnerabilities: `uv run pip-audit`
- Lint: `uv run ruff check src/ tests/` and `uv run ruff format src/ tests/`
- Types: `uv run ty check src/`
- Property tests: `uv run pytest` (Hypothesis configured); browser end-to-end uses Playwright MCP.

## Project conventions
- Python via uv (never pip directly); package manager discipline per skills/modern_python.md.
- Privacy-first: no third-party trackers/analytics in web frontends; prefer OpenStreetMap
  over Google Maps; audit data flows per skills/security_audit.md.
- Web frontend changes follow `.cline/skills/frontend-design/SKILL.md` principles
  (distinctive, intentional design; avoid templated AI-default aesthetics).
